---
/**
 * GrainOverlay.astro — DESIGN.md §4.
 *
 * A full-page noise overlay on every public page. This is what separates
 * "editorial" from "dashboard": subtle enough that you only notice it when it
 * is gone.
 *
 * Inline SVG feTurbulence fractal noise. No image request, no external asset,
 * no canvas, no JavaScript. `position: fixed`, `pointer-events: none`, and
 * `mix-blend-mode: overlay`, with the opacity driven by --grain-opacity so the
 * two modes are tuned INDEPENDENTLY — `overlay` against warm off-white behaves
 * nothing like `overlay` against near-black, and one value does not carry.
 *
 * Presence on every public page is a §9 quality-floor item.
 */
---

<div class="grain-overlay" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg width="100%" height="100%" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <filter id="grain-noise">
      <feTurbulence
        type="fractalNoise"
        baseFrequency="0.82"
        numOctaves="3"
        stitchTiles="stitch"
      />
      <feColorMatrix type="saturate" values="0" />
    </filter>
    <rect width="100%" height="100%" filter="url(#grain-noise)" />
  </svg>
</div>
